Subject: input: Return accepts the on-screen keyboard's text

inputTextHandler() has cases for Backspace, Escape and CTRL+V and none for
Return, so the accept branch at src/game/menuitem.c:1583 (result == 1) is
unreachable from a keyboard. On a desktop that only means the key does nothing.

On iOS it traps the player. Creating a profile offers "type with the iOS
keyboard" (menuitem.c row 5 -> inputStartTextInput), and a software keyboard's
only dismiss affordance is its own Return key — there is no Escape, and the
game's own on-screen OK is underneath the keyboard. SDL sends the scancode
(SDL_uikitviewcontroller.m textFieldShouldReturn) and nothing consumed it, so
the dialog could be typed into and never left: force-quit (the user, on device,
2026-09-14). The other half of the fix is SDL_HINT_RETURN_KEY_HIDES_IME in
app/ios/pd_ios_main.m, which is what actually lowers the keyboard.

Not PLATFORM_IOS-guarded: Return accepting a text field is right everywhere, and
this is on the list of fixes to offer upstream (Q-002).

diff --git a/port/src/input.c b/port/src/input.c
index 6bc04fec8..e0dc3d5cb 100644
--- a/port/src/input.c
+++ b/port/src/input.c
@@ -2165,6 +2165,19 @@ s32 inputTextHandler(char *out, const u32 outSize, s32 *curCol, s32 oskCharsOnly
 		}
 	} else if (key == VK_ESCAPE) {
 		return -1;
+	} else if (key == VK_RETURN) {
+		// Accept, which menuitem.c:1583 turns into "OK was pressed": it moves
+		// the on-screen keyboard's cursor to OK, presses it, and calls
+		// inputStopTextInput().
+		//
+		// Upstream has no case for Return here at all, which on a desktop only
+		// means the key does nothing. On iOS it is the bug that traps the
+		// player: the software keyboard's only dismiss affordance IS its Return
+		// key (there is no Escape and no hardware key), SDL sends the scancode
+		// and nothing consumes it, so a new-profile dialog could be typed into
+		// and never left. SDL_HINT_RETURN_KEY_HIDES_IME (pd_ios_main.m) hides
+		// the keyboard; this is what makes the name stick.
+		return 1;
 	}
 
 	return 0;
